So, I have decided that I want to attempt creating this dream with other like minded individuals. 
I want to firstly make it clear that I am in no way an expert of game development. 
However I have been working with engines like Godot and Unitiy for the past 4 years.
That being said I also dont expect anyone else to be an expert. 
That being said you should be able to communicate effectively and work with others without abuse or negativity.
After all if you are here you are likely a fan as well.

I will be listing what I believe is needed to make this work. If there is something 
I am missing or maybe mistaken on I am always open to being corrected and educated.

1. Game Designer / Creative Director

- Defines the game's vision, genre and identity.
- Designs gameplay mechanics and systems.
- Creates levels, progression and challenges.
- Balances difficulty, pacing and player experience.
- Makes decisions about what belongs in the game.

2. Programmer / Developer

- Implements gameplay mechanics.
- Builds player movement, combat and interactions.
- Implements enemy AI and game systems.
- Handles physics, collision and animations.
- Manages saving, menus and technical performance.
Typically works in Unity, Godot or GameMaker.

3. 2D Artist / Visual Artist

- Designs characters, enemies and environments.
- Creates sprites, backgrounds and objects.
- Establishes the visual style and colour palette.
- Produces visual effects and UI artwork.
- Ensures consistency across the game's visuals.

4. 2D Animator

- Animates character movement.
- Creates attack, damage and death animations.
- Animates enemies and environmental objects.
- Adds movement and personality to the game.

5. Sound Designer / Composer

- Creates music and atmosphere.
- Produces sound effects for movement, combat and interactions.
- Designs environmental audio.
- Handles audio mixing and implementation.

6. Level Designer

Can be combined with game designer
- Builds playable levels and environments.
- Designs enemy encounters and obstacles.
- Controls difficulty progression.
- Creates exploration opportunities and secrets.
- Ensures levels feel engaging and rewarding.

7. QA Tester / Playtester

- Finds bugs and technical problems.
- Tests gameplay mechanics.
- Identifies frustrating or confusing sections.
- Checks difficulty and game balance.
- Tests different hardware and resolutions.
